{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/1792048194304-engineer-8e-fix1.report.md; sed -n '40,175p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; rg -n 'semantic-bytecode-.*(nan|metadata)|not= value|dao.jing' test/yin/vm_test.cljc; rg -n 'Known limitation|same-content|Two nodes' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-15 07:09:54 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-15 14:09:54 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a13e5c-17cf-7bc0-8386-9c5cc0fd27de\n\n# 8e fix round 1 — exact ruling implemented; ruling premises fail on JVM\n\nThe requested implementation and tests are present, uncommitted and unstaged. **The required green gates are not achieved.** The exact prescribed leaf rule does not recognize boxed JVM NaNs, and the prescribed T3 inputs have distinct addresses in this worktree. These require a revised architect instruction; I did not substitute a different leaf rule or weaken the tests.\n\n## Changes and preservation\n\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`: private `same-meta?` renamed to `same-content?`; exact leaf rule `(or (= a b) (and (not= a a) (not= b b)))`; map/set/sequential count checks, map `contains?` before `find`, metadata comparison and recursive metadata rule retained; guard uses the new predicate, with collision message and ex-data unchanged. Added the specified NaN docstring sentence and NaN key/set scope boundary.\n- `test/yin/vm_test.cljc`: T1–T3 beside structural sharing. T1 pins `:segment/blake3-88491ea0d131d67ecf50c6a1714868257c996f9518a139262e049ebd428e55b7`. NaNs use `(* 1.0 ##NaN)` and `(* -1.0 ##NaN)`; no unary minus introduced.\n- P2-1: `rg -n 'resolved-of|last-resolved' src test` initially found only the helper and atom definitions/internal references; deleted both and their now-unused requires. Final rg has no matches.\n- Optional P3-2/P3-3: replaced stale lowerer/deleted-namespace prose and added the missing final newline in debruijn_register_code_test. P3-5: removed the two leftover blank lines in linker_test. Skipped P3-1's wider require formatting.\n- SHA-256 comparison against the initial dirty/deleted tracked paths confirms only test_utils.cljc, debruijn_register_code_test.cljc and linker_test.cljc changed among those existing paths. All other prior dirty/deleted paths remain byte-identical/deleted. The only newly modified tracked files are vm.cljc and vm_test.cljc. No docs, src/yang, or semantic/linearize/code.cljc edit. No staging or commit; staged diff empty. `git diff --check` passes.\n\n## Mutant proof\n\nTemporarily replaced only `(not (same-content? prior row))` with `(not (= prior row))`, then ran:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -n yin.vm-test -v yin.vm-test/semantic-bytecode-nan-structural-sharing\n```\n\nExit 1: **1 test, 1 assertion, 0 failures, 1 error**, `Semantic bytecode address collision` at the pinned NaN id. T1 kills host `=`. Restored the saved fixed vm.cljc bytes and asserted byte equality immediately afterward. This mutant result does **not** prove the prescribed replacement works: it fails independently, as below.\n\n## Verification (foreground, sequential)\n\nLogs: `collab/1792047012394-engineer-8e-fix1-verification/`.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| kondo, vm.cljc, vm_test.cljc and all 43 modified surviving Clojure source/test paths | Exit 0; **0 errors, 0 warnings**. One informational unused excluded `eval` in stack.cljc. `kondo-final.log` |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm-test` | Exit 1; **36 tests, 484 assertions, 1 failure, 2 errors**. `vm-test.log` |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.int-ops-test -e :slow` | Exit 1; **13 tests, 49 assertions, 4 failures, 0 errors**. `int-ops.log` |\n| Full 35-namespace changed command below | Exit 1; **35 selected namespaces, 34 with quick tests, 631 tests, 13,155 assertions, 4 failures, 0 errors**. `changed-quick.log` |\n| Whole yin.vm quick tier, including UCF and vm-test | Exit 1; **104 namespaces, 1,874 tests, 32,327 assertions, 1 failure, 3 errors**. `vm-quick.log` |\n\nKondo command (also repeated after the final whitespace cleanup):\n\n```sh\nclj -M:kondo --config '{:output {:summary true}}' --lint src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc test/yin/vm_test.cljc $(git diff --name-only --diff-filter=ACM -- '*.clj' '*.cljc' '*.cljs')\n```\n\nFull changed command, rerun after implementation:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.e2e-c2-test -n yang.python.antlr.e2e-test -n yang.python.antlr.float-address-test -n yang.python.antlr.int-contract-test -n yang.python.antlr.int-heap-test -n yang.python.antlr.int-literal-test -n yang.python.antlr.int-ops-test -n yang.python.antlr.prelude-parity-test -n yang.python.antlr.safepoint-test -n yin.repl.require-test -n yin.vm.attach-image-test -n yin.vm.cell-test -n yin.vm.continuation-invoke-test -n yin.vm.data-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.register-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-effects-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-parity-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects-test -n yin.vm.effect-forgery-test -n yin.vm.engine-gate-test -n yin.vm.ffi-test -n yin.vm.heap-reclamation-test -n yin.vm.host-typed-values-test -n yin.vm.integer-test -n yin.vm.linker.cross-host-transfer-test -n yin.vm.linker.dht-test -n yin.vm.linker.remote-transfer-test -n yin.vm.linker-manifest-test -n yin.vm.linker-test -n yin.vm.rule-r-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test -n yin.vm.stream-poll-test -e :slow\n```\n\nWhole VM command:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -r '^yin\\.vm(?:\\..*|-test)$' -e :slow\n```\n\nT4 `yang.python.antlr.float-address-test` remains green in the changed-namespace gate. The four changed-gate/T5 failures are `nan-comparisons-test` and `float-division-edge-test` on stack and register. The broad VM result comprises the three new regression-test failures/errors plus `yin.vm.linker.head-board-test/the-board-crosses-a-real-loopback-socket`: `java.net.SocketException: Operation not permitted` at the real socket bind. The loopback case was attempted; the sandbox does not permit it. No escalation or approval rejection occurred.\n\n## Blocking evidence for the architect\n\n`premises.log` records a direct JVM diagnostic:\n\n1. Primitive NaN locals give `(not= a a)` true, but passing those values into `(fn [a b] [(= a b) (not= a a) (not= b b)])` yields **`[false false false]`**. Generic boxed argument self-comparison takes JVM identity equality. Accordingly `same-content?` returns false for the two separately produced NaNs, and T1/T2 throw. The stored row-slot assertion `(not= v v)` also returns false on JVM, independently of the guard.\n2. The requested metadata-bearing literal values retain their metadata and mint **different** ids:\n   - meaning 1: `:segment/blake3-813c887f00269e32f2ae946f572b385fe1e9efcf5e0614833e2369b6667dd1d1`\n   - meaning 2: `:segment/blake3-72250312db47333253f9462d4c3ca66c87637e3de368abf0ad05933d202aaeb3`\n   Therefore the exact T3 AST does not collide and does not throw. The metadata predicate itself correctly returns false for those two values.\n\nA revised portable NaN leaf/test rule and a revised T3 collision fixture are needed before these gates can pass. The mandated docstring statements were added as instructed; the evidence above contradicts their claimed behavior in this worktree. No addressing/encoder change was made to force the ruling's premises true.\n\nNode/Dart verification remains the orchestrator's gate per the ruling; neither lane was run here. P2-2/P2-3 documentation follow-ups remain assigned to the orchestrator; docs stayed frozen.\n\nBLOCKED\n\n(defprotocol IVM\n  \"Unified VM protocol for execution, evaluation, and observable state.\"\n\n  (step\n    [vm]\n    \"Execute one step of already-loaded work. An idle VM is returned\n     unchanged; program input arrives through an attached stream observer.\")\n\n  (run\n    [vm]\n    \"Run already-loaded work until halted or blocked.\")\n\n  (eval\n    [vm ast]\n    \"Convert and evaluate a supplied AST. Does not drain any independently\n     queued program input; explicit observer coordination does that.\")\n\n  (reset\n    [vm]\n    \"Reset execution state to a known initial state, preserving loaded program.\")\n\n  (halted?\n    [vm]\n    \"Returns true if VM has halted (completed or error).\")\n\n  (blocked?\n    [vm]\n    \"Returns true if VM is blocked waiting for external input.\")\n\n  (value\n    [vm]\n    \"Returns the current result value, or nil if not yet computed.\"))\n\n\n(defprotocol IVMState\n  \"CESK state accessor protocol.\n   Exposes the four components of the CESK machine model.\n   Representations are VM-specific but the structure is universal.\"\n\n  (control\n    [vm]\n    \"Returns the current control state (what is being evaluated).\n     VM-specific: AST node, instruction pointer, node ID, etc.\")\n\n  (environment\n    [vm]\n    \"Returns the current lexical environment (variable bindings).\")\n\n  (store\n    [vm]\n    \"Returns the current store (heap/global state).\")\n\n  (continuation\n    [vm]\n    \"Returns the current continuation (what to do next).\n     VM-specific: linked frames, stack vector, call-stack, etc.\"))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Rule R: the definition operator is syntax, never a name\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def definition-operator\n  \"The one name that is syntax rather than a name: the operator of a\n   definition `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)`. It is legal only as the\n   operator of a two-operand application whose first operand is a literal\n   symbol other than itself. It is never a binder, a store key, a\n   definition key, a macro name, or a primitive.\"\n  'yin/def)\n\n\n(def reserved-names\n  \"The reserved set: a one-entry contract table. `require` is dynamic and\n   stays an ordinary primitive.\"\n  #{definition-operator})\n\n\n(defn reserved-name?\n  [x]\n  (contains? reserved-names x))\n\n\n(defn reserved-name-defect\n  \"The data of a Rule R refusal: `role` names where the reserved name\n   appeared (`:variable`, `:binder`, `:store-key`, `:definition-key`,\n   `:definition-shape`, `:primitive`, `:env`, `:store`, `:macro`,\n   `:registry`).\"\n  [role name]\n  {:rule :reserved-name, :name name, :role role})\n\n\n(defn refuse-reserved!\n  \"Throw the Rule R refusal for `name` in `role`, merged with `data`.\"\n  ([role name] (refuse-reserved! role name {}))\n  ([role name data]\n   (throw (ex-info (str \"Reserved name \" name \" used as \"\n                        (clojure.core/name role))\n                   (merge data (reserved-name-defect role name))))))\n\n\n(defn check-params!\n  \"Refuse a lambda's binders where they would bind: a reserved name\n   (Rule R), and any binder that is not a symbol, refused as\n   `:non-symbol-parameter` with the binder's coarse `:kind`. A keyword\n   parameter would otherwise write any key into a named kernel's\n   environment, `:yin.k/store-of` included. `data` is merged into the\n   refusal. Returns `params`.\"\n  ([params] (check-params! params {}))\n  ([params data]\n   (when-let [p (some #(when (reserved-name? %) %) params)]\n     (refuse-reserved! :binder p data))\n   ;; the bad binder is boxed: a nil or false binder must not read as none\n   (when-let [[p] (some #(when-not (symbol? %) [%]) params)]\n     (throw (ex-info \"Lambda parameter is not a symbol\"\n                     (merge data\n                            {:reason :non-symbol-parameter,\n                             :kind (values/kind-of p)}))))\n   params))\n\n\n(defn check-bindings!\n  \"Refuse a supplied map (an env, a store, a registry) that binds a\n   reserved name. Returns `m`.\"\n  [role m]\n  (when (map? m)\n    (when-let [n (some #(when (reserved-name? %) %) (keys m))]\n      (refuse-reserved! role n)))\n  m)\n\n\n(defn definition-operator?\n  \"True when a map AST node is the variable naming the definition\n   operator.\"\n  [node]\n  (and (= :variable (:type node)) (= definition-operator (:name node))))\n6:            [dao.jing :as jing]\n438:(deftest semantic-bytecode-list-payloads-mint-no-metadata\n484:(deftest semantic-bytecode-nan-structural-sharing\n494:    (is (not= value value))))\n497:(deftest semantic-bytecode-nested-nan-structural-sharing\n505:(deftest semantic-bytecode-scalar-metadata-collision\n628:(deftest semantic-bytecode-sharing-refuses-to-merge-distinct-metadata\n633:      ;; dao.jing's canonical CBOR encoding hashes symbol metadata, so the\n690:(deftest semantic-bytecode-compares-metadata-inside-metadata\n709:(deftest semantic-bytecode-strips-reader-positions-inside-metadata\n719:      ;; dao.jing's canonical encoding refuses metadata on a metadata map\n720:      ;; (dao.jing.cbor.md ruling A3), so such a literal cannot be\n735:   (deftest semantic-bytecode-strips-reader-generated-positions-in-metadata\n749:(deftest semantic-bytecode-nodes-vector-metadata-is-refused\n1142:(defn- same-content?\n1145:   map's own metadata, compares through `same-content?` too). `=` alone ignores\n1161:       (or (nil? (meta a)) (same-content? (meta a) (meta b)))\n1167:                                            (and (same-content? k k')\n1168:                                                 (same-content? v v')))))\n1173:                                     (same-content? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b)))\n1177:                                  (every? true? (map same-content? a b)))\n1193:   Known limitation, inherited from `dao.jing` and not fixed here: the\n1228:                      (not (same-content? prior row)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
